en:
Reflectors (catadiottri) are plastic devices that reflect light; their function is to indicate the presence and size of the vehicles on which they are fitted.

When lit up, they make vehicles and trailers that are parked (or broken down) on the road more visible, especially at night, even with their lights off.

They can be:

- white if at the front (also on trailers or semi-trailers);

- red if at the rear; these are compulsory for all vehicles and trailers;

- triangular in shape only at the rear of trailers, semi-trailers and small trailers (carrelli);

- yellow if on the sides, to mark trailers, semi-trailers, small trailers and vehicles of considerable length, i.e. those longer than 6 metres.
